# Legal Agentic RAG App (Text Mining Project)

This project implements and evaluates different RAG architectures (Single-Agent, Multi-Agent, and Hybrid) applied to a multi-nation legal corpus (Italy, Estonia, Slovenia). It also includes an automated evaluation pipeline using the RAGAS framework.

---

## LOCAL VERSION (NO DOCKER)

# 0) Go to the project folder
cd path/to/agentic_rag_app

# 1) Create and activate the virtual environment
# --- Windows (PowerShell / CMD)
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate

# --- Linux / macOS
# python -m venv venv
# source venv/bin/activate

# 2) Install dependencies
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3) Configure the .env file
# Create a file named .env in the project root and insert your API keys. 
# This project uses models via OpenRouter and Groq to handle evaluation limits:
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key

# 4) Run the Streamlit application
streamlit run app.py

# 5) Interface Navigation (http://localhost:8501)
#   - Chatbot Q&A: Interact with the Single-Agent or the Multi-Agent Supervisor.
#   - RAG Evaluation: Run RAGAS metrics (Faithfulness, Context Precision/Recall, Answer Relevancy).

---

## DOCKER VERSION

# 0) Go to the project folder
cd path/to/agentic_rag_app

# 1) Build the Docker image
docker build -t agentic-rag-app .

# 2) Ensure the .env file is present in the project root (with OpenRouter/Groq keys)

# 3) Prepare data on the HOST computer (outside the container), for example:
# /path/on/host/legal_corpus/
#   italy/
#   estonia/
#   slovenia/

# 4) Run the container (mounting local data into the /data folder inside the container)
docker run -p 8501:8501 \
  --env-file .env \
  -v /path/on/host/legal_corpus:/data \
  agentic-rag-app